TITANIC: COMPLETE TRAINING PLAN (CLEAN VERSION)
Comprehensive EDA + Preprocessing + Modeling Curriculum
With Pandas & Polars Coverage
________________________________________
1. Data Ingestion and Schema Validation
1.1 Data Loading
•	Load CSV dataset using default inference
•	Load with explicit dtype enforcement (pandas dtype= / polars schema=)
•	Load with intentionally incorrect types and correct coercions
•	Validate CSV parsing (quotes, embedded commas, encoding issues)
1.2 Initial Structure Inspection
•	Inspect shape, column names, dtypes
•	Inspect index meaning and reassign index if needed
•	Verify schema matches expectations
•	Simulate schema drift (drop or reorder columns)
•	Memory footprint analysis and numeric downcasting
1.3 Granularity and Identity Validation
•	Confirm row-level granularity (one row = one passenger)
•	Check PassengerId uniqueness
•	Validate whether Ticket implies group-level identity
•	Identify latent family and ticket group structures
________________________________________
2. Data Understanding and Semantic Validation
2.1 Column Semantics
•	Validate meanings of Survived, Pclass, Sex, SibSp, Parch, Embarked
•	Identify numerical, categorical, ordinal, and text features
•	Validate ordinal nature of Pclass
•	Validate family size definition and consistency with SibSp + Parch
•	Basic domain rules: 
o	Age >= 0
o	Fare >= 0
2.2 Data Integrity
•	Check logical relationships: 
o	Family structures
o	Fare-per-person consistency within Ticket groups
o	Gender and age patterns
________________________________________
3. Data Quality Assessment
3.1 Missing Data
•	Detect missingness across columns
•	Analyze missingness patterns
•	Compute missingness correlation
•	Missingness clustering
•	Missingness association with target variable
•	Impact of missingness on feature distributions
3.2 Validity Checks
•	Detect invalid categories in Embarked
•	Out-of-range and impossible values
•	Duplicate row detection
•	Duplicate key detection (PassengerId)
•	Cardinality checks for Cabin and Ticket
•	Class imbalance analysis
________________________________________
4. Data Integration and Join Operations
4.1 Pre-Join Analysis
•	Create synthetic lookup tables (Port metadata, Name title mappings)
•	Define join keys and validate key uniqueness
•	Identify join risks and check datatype compatibility
4.2 Join Execution
•	Left join enrichment tables
•	Inner join diagnostics
•	Join indicator column inspection
•	Validate one-to-many and many-to-one joins
4.3 Post-Join Validation
•	Row count reconciliation
•	Null inflation checks
•	Duplicate detection post-join
•	Drop auxiliary columns
________________________________________
5. Target Variable Analysis
•	Class distribution and survival rate
•	Survival rate by Sex, Class, Embarked, Age groups, Family size
•	Baseline model performance estimation
•	Stability of target across folds
•	Business interpretation of false positives vs false negatives
________________________________________
6. Missing Data Handling
•	Drop high-missingness columns (Cabin scenario)
•	Simple imputations: 
o	Mean/median for Age
o	Mode for Embarked
•	Group-aware imputation: 
o	Age by Sex × Pclass
•	Missing indicator features
•	Distribution comparisons pre/post imputation
•	Leakage-aware imputation (within training folds only)
________________________________________
7. Outlier Analysis
•	Fare distribution and high-end outliers
•	IQR method
•	Percentile capping
•	Log transformation of Fare
•	Ticket-level fare aggregation (per-person fare)
•	Age plausibility checks by Class
•	Survival outliers (unexpected outcomes)
________________________________________
8. Statistical Exploration
8.1 Univariate Statistics
•	Measures of central tendency and dispersion
•	Skewness and kurtosis
•	Quantile analysis
•	Value count analysis
8.2 Bivariate and Multivariate
•	Survival vs feature relationships
•	Correlation analysis
•	Cross tabulations
•	Collinearity diagnostics
•	Simpson’s paradox checks
•	Non-linear association checks
8.3 Hypothesis Testing
•	Survival differences by Sex (chi-square)
•	Survival differences by Class (chi-square)
•	Fare differences (t-test or nonparametric test)
•	Multiple testing considerations
8.4 Advanced Statistics
•	Effect size (Cohen’s d, Cramér’s V)
•	Confidence intervals for survival rates
•	Bootstrap resampling for stability analysis
•	Permutation tests for feature relevance
________________________________________
9. Visualization Tasks
9.1 Core EDA Visualizations
•	Histograms for Age, Fare
•	Boxplots for Age/Fare vs Survived
•	KDE plots for Age and Fare
•	Bar charts for categorical features
•	Pair plots
•	Correlation heatmaps
9.2 Faceted and Groupwise Plots
•	Faceted histograms by Survived
•	Survival barplots by Sex × Class
•	Survival heatmaps (Pclass × Sex)
•	KDEs faceted by Survived
9.3 Missingness Visualizations
•	Missingness matrix
•	Missingness heatmap
•	Missingness clustering plots
9.4 Interaction and Advanced Visuals
•	Interaction plots: 
o	Sex × Class
o	Fare × Embarked
•	Partial dependence plots
•	ICE plots
•	Bootstrap distribution plots
•	Effect size visualizations
9.5 Model Diagnostics
•	ROC curve
•	Precision–Recall curve
•	Calibration curve
•	Logistic regression residual plots
•	Feature importance plots
•	SHAP summary and dependence plots
________________________________________
10. Data Transformation
•	Log transformation for Fare
•	Standard scaling
•	Robust scaling
•	Age binning
•	Rank transformation
•	Ensuring invertibility of transformations
________________________________________
11. Text Feature Engineering
From Name
•	Title extraction
•	Rare title consolidation
•	Token counts
•	Length-based features
•	Regex robustness tests
•	Honorific hierarchy validation
From Cabin
•	Deck extraction
•	Cabin presence indicator
•	Cabin group extraction
